1 Introduction
**************

‘apt-man’ is a comprehensive command-line tool for managing APT package
sources, including Ubuntu PPAs and third-party repositories, along with
their GPG signing keys.  It provides an intuitive interface for common
tasks that would otherwise require manual file editing and complex APT
commands.

1.1 Features
============

   • List and categorize all APT sources
   • Enable and disable sources without deleting them
   • Show packages available in or installed from specific sources
   • Bulk upgrade sources between Ubuntu releases
   • Comprehensive GPG key management and validation
   • Support for both legacy .list and modern .sources formats
   • Identify security issues like missing or expired keys


